            &\leq \|x_0-x^*\|^2 \label{eg bounded iterates}
        \end{align}
      where the last inequality comes from our choice of $\nu$. This indicates that our iterates are bounded and allows us to apply (\ref{EG step lower bound}). Note also from rearranging (\ref{eg pre half bound}), we have
      \begin{align}
         (1-C_\nu^2)\|x_k-\hat{x}_k\|^2  &\leq \|x_k-x^*\|^2-\|x_{k+1}-x^*\|^2 \notag\\
         &\overset{(\ref{eg bounded iterates})}{\leq} \| x_0-x^*\|^2 \notag \\
         \Rightarrow \|x_k-\hat{x}_k\|^2&\leq  \frac{\|x_0-x^*\|^2}{1-C_\nu^2} \label{eg half bound}
      \end{align}
      From Young's Inequality and combining (\ref{eg bounded iterates}) and (\ref{eg half bound}), we thus have for any $\beta> 0$
      \begin{align*}
          \|\hat{x}_k-x^*\|^2 &\overset{(\ref{full young})}{\leq} (1+\beta^{-1})\|x_k-x^*\|^2+(1+\beta)\|x_k-\hat{x}_k\|^2 \\  
          &\overset{(\ref{eg half bound})}{\leq} \left( 1+\frac{1}{1-C_\nu^2}+\frac{1}{\beta}+\frac{\beta}{1-C_\nu^2} \right)\|x_0-x^*\|^2 
          \end{align*}
          We choose $\beta=\sqrt{1-C_\nu^2}$ to minimize the upper bound, obtaining the following

          \begin{align*}
          \|\hat{x}_k-x^*\|^2&\leq \left( 1+\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-C_\nu^2}} \right)^2\|x_0-x^*\|^2
      \end{align*}

