\label{lem: finite while loops}
Suppose $F$ is 1-symmetric $(L_0,L_1)$-Lipschitz. Then the total number of while-loop calls of Algorithm~\ref{alg:AdaptiveAlgo} with backtracking parameter $\rho>2$ is at most 
    \begin{equation}
    \label{eqn:linesearch-finite-operator-call-bound}
        N=2\max\left\{
            0, 
            \left\lceil \frac{\log(L_0/\lambda_{-1}^0)}{\log(\rho-1)} \right\rceil,
            \left\lceil \frac{\log(L_1/\lambda_{-1}^1)} {\log(\rho-1)} \right\rceil
        \right\}
    \end{equation}

    Consequently, for all accepted steps we have
    \begin{equation}
        \lambda_k^0 \le \bar{\lambda}_N^0
        =
        \rho^{\lceil N/2 \rceil}\lambda_{-1}^0,
        \qquad
        \lambda_k^1 \le \bar{\lambda}_N^1
        =
        \rho^{\lceil N/2 \rceil}\lambda_{-1}^1. \label{eqn: lam max app}
    \end{equation}

First, if both $\lambda_k^0\geq L_0$ and $\lambda_k^1 \geq L_1$, then from Lemma~\ref{lem:lipschitz analogue} we have
        \begin{equation*}
            \gamma_k\|F(\hat{x}_k)-F(\tilde{x}_k)\|\leq C_\nu\|\hat{x}_k-\tilde{x}_k\|
        \end{equation*}
        where $\tilde{x}_k=x_k$ for  
  \begingroup
  \hypersetup{linkcolor=PineGreen} 
  \hyperref[EG_update]{\color{PineGreen}\sfEG} 
  \endgroup
  \xspace
 and $\hat{x}_{k-1}$ for  
  \begingroup
  \hypersetup{linkcolor=PineGreen} 
  \hyperref[PEG_update]{\color{PineGreen}\sfPEG} 
  \endgroup
  \xspace
. Note that this is the while loop condition for Algorithm~\ref{alg:AdaptiveAlgo}, so once $\lambda_k^0\geq L_0$ and $\lambda_k^1 \geq L_1$, no additional while loop calls will occur. 

       Now, note that at each update step in the while loop, the update factor applied to $\lambda_k^0$ or $\lambda_k^1$ is lower bounded by $\rho-1$ and upper bounded by $\rho$. Thus, after $k$ while-loop calls, the denominator estimates are lower bounded by

    \begin{equation*}
       \lambda_k^0\geq  (\rho-1)^{\lfloor k/2 \rfloor}\lambda_{-1}^0,
        \qquad
        \lambda_k^1\geq(\rho-1)^{\lfloor k/2 \rfloor}\lambda_{-1}^1
    \end{equation*}

    Consequently, by the definition of $N$, we have that
    \begin{equation*}
        \lambda_N^0\geq (\rho-1)^{\left\lceil N/2 \right\rceil}\lambda_{-1}^0\geq L_0,
        \qquad
        \lambda_N^1\geq (\rho-1)^{\left\lceil N/2 \right\rceil}\lambda_{-1}^1\geq L_1.
    \end{equation*}

    At this point, no further while loop calls will occur, leading to at most $N$ while loop calls over all the algorithm's iterations.  The upper bounds bounds on $\lambda_k^0$ and $\lambda_k^1$ follow immediately since both sequences only increase during while-loop calls. As a final note, these bounds on the number of while loop calls imply that over $K$ iterations of each algorithm, there are at most $2K+N$ operator evaluations for {\color{PineGreen}\sfEG-LS}\xspace and $K+N+1$ operator evaluations for {\color{PineGreen}\sfPEG-LS}\xspace.

\label{lem: adaeg step lower bound}
